in every single one of us there is a  void that can never be filled a part of  us that yearns for a complete and  definitive understanding of the life  that engulfs us an omni essent endpoint  in the pursuit of knowledge we possess a  level of consciousness that seemingly  never meets the needs of the reality  that precedes it we are conscious enough  to observe the world ask questions and  make logical summations but we are not  conscious enough to find and sustain  conclusive overarching answers from it  all our most meaningful questions can  only be speculated questions like where  we came from why we are here where we  are going and what is the point of it  all the simple fact is we currently have  no way of finding answers to these  questions perhaps these answers do not  even exist in conclusive form or perhaps  humans are not made with the purpose to  ever find them when reflecting on our  inability to conclusively answer our  most basic existential questions over  the last several hundred thousand years  it begins to feel hopeless and it is our  continuing ignorance of reality that  creates the void that we can never quite  fill it is why we chase distractions and  temporary pleasures in life why we all  sometimes feel lost sad and helpless  because what is the point of living  without answers as to why we live at all  but arguably not having all of the  answers is the greatest reason to live  as humans we operate from a system of  duality that cares about logic and  understanding as well as emotion and  feeling our purpose and enjoyment of  life is not bound exclusively to a  finite endpoint of the pursuit of  knowledge it is also dependent on our  ability to feel the emotion of life's  fluctuation and uncertainty the  perpetual game of cat and mouse that we  play with reality is what gets us  excited and interested to be alive  without it what would there be to strive  for what would there be to be inspired  by the door for creating and searching  for unique meaning in life would close  we should not live with existential  angst or a constant chip on our shoulder  because we do not and cannot possess  definitive answers to all of our  questions instead we should live with  the excitement and Wonder that comes  from the fact that because of this we  will always possess the potential for  new discoveries and new worlds of life  we will always be able to create  theories and meaning and experience the  or of their realizations it is deeply  human to ask questions and work towards  understanding and explanations to  fantasize about the singularity between  humanity and the reality in which it  resides to visualize an end point of  intelligence and become synchronized  with absolute truth but it is also  deeply human to never achieve this and  to believe and depend on it occurring  misses the entire point  the pursuit of knowledge can and should  just exist for itself this pursuit is  what makes us who we are  excitement Wonder and humanity itself  are all rooted in the very fact that  life or at least our understanding of it  is constantly in flux and we can always  learn something new about it if we view  life in this way the void we all have  within us we'll begin to feel a little  less deep thank you for watching if we  found enjoyment and value in this video  please give it a thumbs up share your  thoughts in the comments below and if  you are not already be sure to subscribe  to our Channel  we are constantly coming out with new  videos to help you experience life with  clarity and Wonder
 

